    "preamble": "Dabur India Limited vs Union Of India & Ors on 17 September, 2025 17-09-2025 Item Nos.46 & 47 In The High Court At Calcutta Subrata Constitutional Writ Jurisdiction Bhattacharyya Appellate Side Ar(C) Wpa No.26167 of 2024 Dabur India Limited -vs- Union of India & Ors. with Wpa No.8975 of 2025 Mr. Sudipto Sarkar, Sr. Adv. Mr. Sourajit Dasgupta Mr. Sudhakar Prasad Mr. Nilanjan Banerjee ...for the petitioner Ms. Vineeta Meharia, sr. adv. Mr. Amit Meharia Ms. Pannistha Singh Ms. Paramita Banerjee Mr. Rohan Raj ...for the respondent nos.2-4 1. It has been submitted by the learned senior counsel for the petitioner that as shelf life of the subject batch of the product in respect of which prohibitory order and thereafter recall order was passed by the Fssai has expired, accordingly, the writ petitions have become infructuous.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "It has been submitted by the learned senior counsel for the petitioner that as shelf life of the subject batch of the product in respect of which prohibitory order and thereafter recall order was passed by the Fssai has expired, accordingly, the writ petitions have become infructuous.",
